    "id": "rate_half_ca_hankel_a1_core_one_exceptional_only_distance_three_complement_residue_rank_three_gate",
    "title": "Rate-half distance-three complement-residue rank-three gate",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "proof",
    "statement": "On the official pair-Lagrange external design, let I be the internal-slope locator, P_Z the external-slope locator, G_x the monic supported-slope locator of an active outside row, and H_x=P_Z/G_x. The 6e+3 residue classes H_x mod I span dimension at most three. Equivalently, both the complement-evaluation matrix H_x(xi_i) and inverse-locator matrix G_x(0)/G_x(xi_i) have rank at most three. The full complement polynomials span dimension at most e+4. Exact biregularity alone does not imply these gates.",
